quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  112,1,"(O Esteemed Messenger!) Proclaim: ‘He is Allah, Who is the One."
  112,2,"Allah is the Transcendent of all, the Protector and Far-Superior to all."
  112,3,"He has not begotten any, nor is He begotten."
  112,4,Nor is there anyone equal to Him.’
  113,1,"Beseech: ‘I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak (or Who brought the universe into existence with an explosion extremely fast),"
  113,2,"From the evil influence (and harmfulness) of everything that He has created,"
  113,3,"And (in particular) from the evil of the murky night when (its) darkness prevails,"
  113,4,"And from the evil of those women (and men) who practise magic on knots by blowing,"
  113,5,And from the mischief of every envious person when he envies.’
  114,1,"Beseech: ‘I seek refuge with the Lord of (the whole of) mankind,"
  114,2,"Who is the King of (all) mankind,"
  114,3,"Who is the God of the (whole) human race,"
  114,4,"From the evil of the slinking whisperer (Satan) who hides himself withdrawing (from the influence of Allah’s remembrance),"
  114,5,"Who whispers into the hearts of mankind,"
  114,6,Whether he (the whispering Satan) comes from the jinn or mankind.’
